WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.564 --> 00:00:11.028
"Today we're going to turn our old crayons into rainbow candles," Miss Shelly said.

2
00:00:11.208 --> 00:00:12.609
She held up a colorful, striped candle.

3
00:00:13.329 --> 00:00:18.191
Nina looked into her bag of old, broken crayons.

4
00:00:31.604 --> 00:00:35.086
She wasn't sure she wanted her purple crayons in a rainbow candle.

5
00:00:35.106 --> 00:00:39.548
"First let's see what colors we have," said Miss Shelly.

6
00:00:40.389 --> 00:00:43.451
The kids emptied their bags of crayons onto the table.

7
00:00:43.471 --> 00:00:52.355
"We've got red, orange, yellow, blue, green, and lots of purple from Nina!"

8
00:00:52.716 --> 00:00:53.656
Miss Shelly said.

9
00:00:53.676 --> 00:00:56.298
"Perfect for rainbow candles."

10
00:00:57.698 --> 00:00:58.879
Nina raised her hand.

11
00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:02.645
"Miss Shelly, can I make a purple candle?

12
00:01:03.606 --> 00:01:05.367
I don't want a rainbow candle."

13
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.188
Miss Shelly paused.

14
00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.850
"Well, we're all going to share crayons.

15
00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.312
If you only want purple, it may be a short candle.

16
00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:15.953
Is that okay?"

17
00:01:17.134 --> 00:01:18.034
Nina nodded.

18
00:01:18.755 --> 00:01:21.216
"Uh-huh. As long as it's purple."

19
00:01:21.236 --> 00:01:27.360
"Okay. First we need to peel the paper off the crayons," Miss Shelly said.

20
00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:31.553
"We don't want the paper in our candles."

21
00:01:32.893 --> 00:01:35.815
When the kids were done, Miss Shelly lit the hot plate.

22
00:01:37.956 --> 00:01:40.737
"Now we'll melt the crayons, one color at a time.

23
00:01:41.377 --> 00:01:43.958
We'll melt them in this top pot," she said.

24
00:01:43.978 --> 00:01:47.119
"Red crayons please."

25
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:51.621
The kids dropped handfuls of red crayons into the pot.

26
00:01:55.683 --> 00:01:56.623
"Ooh, they're melting!"

27
00:01:57.104 --> 00:01:57.844
Jason said.

28
00:01:58.668 --> 00:01:59.488
"Be careful.

29
00:02:00.229 --> 00:02:01.810
The pot is very hot!"

30
00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.170
Miss Shelly warned.

31
00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:07.432
"Now we pour the wax into your glass jars.

32
00:02:08.353 --> 00:02:11.274
Carefully hold the wick in the center of your jar like this.

33
00:02:12.254 --> 00:02:13.155
I'll pour the wax.

34
00:02:14.015 --> 00:02:15.636
Do not let go of your wick!"

35
00:02:15.996 --> 00:02:16.917
Miss Shelly said.

36
00:02:18.157 --> 00:02:23.480
She poured a layer of red wax into the bottom of Izzie's jar, Jason's jar, and then Bobby's

37
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:29.020
jar. She did the same for orange, yellow, green, and blue wax.

38
00:02:31.161 --> 00:02:32.262
Nina just watched.

39
00:02:33.223 --> 00:02:34.324
Her jar was empty.

40
00:02:34.344 --> 00:02:36.546
"Here we go.

41
00:02:37.206 --> 00:02:39.588
The last layer," Miss Shelly said.

42
00:02:40.489 --> 00:02:42.610
Nina jumped up and held out her jar.

43
00:02:43.471 --> 00:02:45.453
Finally they were ready for purple!

44
00:02:47.314 --> 00:02:49.716
Miss Shelly poured everyone some purple wax.

45
00:02:53.959 --> 00:02:58.955
Shelly, my candle doesn't reach the top of my jar," Nina said, frowning.

46
00:02:58.975 --> 00:03:03.318
"Nina, I warned you about that," Miss Shelly said.

47
00:03:03.338 --> 00:03:04.479
"I know.

48
00:03:04.499 --> 00:03:07.801
But I didn't think it was going to look like this!"

49
00:03:08.361 --> 00:03:09.042
Nina said.

50
00:03:09.902 --> 00:03:13.705
She looked sadly at her short candle with its long, droopy wick.

51
00:03:13.725 --> 00:03:17.768
"I've still got some red crayons," Bobby said.

52
00:03:17.788 --> 00:03:21.110
"And Jason has blue crayons.

53
00:03:21.771 --> 00:03:23.452
Red and blue make purple.

54
00:03:24.136 --> 00:03:26.118
We can make more purple wax."

55
00:03:26.738 --> 00:03:28.220
Bobby looked at Miss Shelly.

56
00:03:29.801 --> 00:03:31.202
Nina smiled at Bobby.

57
00:03:31.222 --> 00:03:33.284
"Thanks," she said.

58
00:03:33.824 --> 00:03:35.145
Sometimes he was nice.

59
00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.809
They melted the red and blue crayons together in the pot.

60
00:03:48.336 --> 00:03:49.217
think that will do.

61
00:03:50.058 --> 00:03:50.578
Don't you?"

62
00:03:51.059 --> 00:03:52.340
Miss Shelly asked Nina.

63
00:03:53.512 --> 00:03:56.414
Nina's candle wasn't as tall as the rainbow candles.

64
00:03:57.115 --> 00:03:59.576
But now it almost reached the top of her jar.

65
00:03:59.596 --> 00:04:03.039
"Yeah. It's better," she said.

66
00:04:06.622 --> 00:04:09.223
Later Miss Shelly trimmed everyone's wicks.

67
00:04:09.924 --> 00:04:12.346
Then she lit the candles and turned off the lights.

68
00:04:14.427 --> 00:04:17.009
Everyone's candles flickered brightly in the dark.

69
00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:19.811
"Our candles look awesome!"

70
00:04:20.211 --> 00:04:21.012
Jason said.

71
00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.643
"Your rainbow candle is really pretty," Nina told Izzie.

72
00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:29.788
"Thanks. Your purple one is too," Izzie said.

73
00:04:30.788 --> 00:04:34.692
Nina looked at her Kids Central friends and teacher in the glowing lights.

74
00:04:36.074 --> 00:04:38.216
She couldn't imagine school without them!
